WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.120
(crowd cheering) - All right,

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.224
let's get ya something that's trending

00:00:02.224 --> 00:00:04.500
in the social media world, sure
to bring you a little bliss.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.405
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:09.190
(uplifting music)

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.800
A female CEO is working hard
to help little girls dream big,

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.980
and she's inspiring them
through a giant Dallas exhibit

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.820
featuring more than 120
life-size statues of real women

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.770
working in the field of STEM.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.630
It's part of a brilliant
initiative called If Then.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.700
Let's say hi to Nicole
Small, who's standing

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.744
in the middle of the exhibit now.

00:00:28.744 --> 00:00:29.577
(crowd applause) She watches our show

00:00:29.577 --> 00:00:33.610
on NBC 5 Dallas-Fort Worth
at two. What's up Fort Worth?

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:34.443
Hey what's up?

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.900
This is amazing. So please tell us more

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.670
about the If Then initiative.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.503
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:40.503 --> 00:00:42.740
We are so happy to be coming
to you here from Dallas.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.047
I'm Nicole Small, Lyda
Hill Philanthropies,

00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:47.050
and we are thrilled to
tell you more about the

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.250
If Then movement that was
started a couple of years ago,

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.010
because we believe if you
can see it, you can be it.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.190
And we know, like you,
you've got a daughter,

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.060
I've got a daughter, lots
of people watching today

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.540
have daughters. And we know
that if we show little girls

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.980
incredible role models,
doing amazing things,

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.080
that those little girls too
will know that they can grow up

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.170
and change the world. And that's
what If Then is all about.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:07.840
And while we were
developing this initiative,

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.730
we were doing TikTok channels
and TV shows and fixing

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.041
museum walls. We came
across an amazing statistic.

00:01:13.041 --> 00:01:15.080
We did not know, and I
don't know if you do,

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.420
but we didn't know that
there are only six statues

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.710
of women in the top 10 cities in the US.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.510
So, you know, like you were from Texas

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.692
and we decided we were
going to go big or go home.

00:01:23.692 --> 00:01:24.525
- Yes.

00:01:24.525 --> 00:01:26.130
- So instead of just fixing it by a few,

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:31.110
we decided to 3D scan
120 amazing STEM women,

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.410
which is what you're seeing behind me.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.110
And one of those amazing
scientists is literally standing

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.200
right next to me. This
is Dr. Danielle Twum.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.740
Some of you might recognize her,

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.120
Kelly cause she was on
your show not too long ago.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.610
She's a cancer biologist and
she is going to change how we

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.350
deal with cancer for
generations. She's incredible.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:51.350
And also behind me is Victoria.
She is a climate scientist.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.470
We all know that that's a really
important issue right now.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.510
She's also a National Geographic explorer.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:57.970
And standing next to her is Kristen,

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.340
Kristen Lear is a bat conservationist.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.314
And they are just a few of
the incredible, amazing women

00:02:03.314 --> 00:02:06.070
that are doing things to
change our world every day.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.520
- Absolutely. (crowd cheering)

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.484
And I'm just saying,
they are all orange, so

00:02:11.484 --> 00:02:14.190
if you were going to have a
theme song, This Girl is on Fire

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:16.020
would be appropriate. Is all I'm saying.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.630
I think that would be a great song to play

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:18.830
while you're out there.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.102
You can catch the exhibit

00:02:20.102 --> 00:02:20.935
- Totally.

00:02:20.935 --> 00:02:23.360
- October 24th at North
Park Center in Dallas.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.870
Thank you so much, Nicole. I'm
liking your posts right now,

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.760
and that's not all our season
long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.180
the go-to pen of the Kelly
Clarkson show wants to honor

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.410
ultimate overachievers just
like you ma'am so they will be

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:38.330
using their G2 gelling pen to
write the If Then initiative,

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.807
a check for a thousand
dollars. How does that sound?

00:02:40.807 --> 00:02:42.896
- [Nicole] Wow that's awesome!

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.703
- [Kelly] Aw, thank you so much.

